diff --git a/proposals/payment-request/README.md b/proposals/payment-request/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/proposals/payment-request/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Payment Request implements the measured default headless profile: no payment app or service is installed. Construction performs actual data conversion and validation, retains ID/shipping state, and creates genuine selected-VM public values over the existing pinned EventTarget/Event backend. Capability queries resolve false; first show closes the request and rejects NotSupportedError; later operations reject InvalidStateError. abort always rejects without closing a newly created request. There are no successful payments, fabricated approvals, receipts, or PaymentResponse instances.
+
+The selected VM owns the constructor functions, request/event wrappers, promises, TypeErrors/RangeErrors, and DOMExceptions. A Host WeakMap holds request/event state, UUIDs come from actual crypto.randomUUID(), methodDetails retains its actual supplied object, and successful allocation registers private platform provenance. Borrowed methods return values/errors in the method's realm; retained removed-frame requests continue to work as measured. Real EventTarget dispatch handles listeners and handlers, including return-false cancellation and handler re-registration order. Secure exposure uses the private document/creator origin snapshot, including in isolated worlds; workers do not expose these interfaces.
+
+Native reference executable SHA256: 9dec394124212f796724d4d32737ba66fdf0319ae6faaf8a1df8cccb4a70e23f. Pinned payment_request.html SHA256: 1d3ca14a4c13a6d9de24dcf68ab2001cb902fd0ba5a83d46f47714e302dc10dd. Unmodified testing.js SHA256: 23e2ebbd851e64a68b1e357a38ed2e6d5d5f72217cb2e14671c4d3eecf6c861b. Source commit: 948d773786380bae36f046639fc61e2ddddd212a. Fixture registration uses default iframe+worker loading; both are explicitly enabled here. No live merchant/payment service was contacted.
+
+Native raw evidence comprises 242 control rows across primary, validation, state-events, conversion, contexts, and extra reports. Additional native-utility-v2.json records actual isolated-world behavior plus an HTTP worker exposure result. Each report binds its expression/driver and executable by SHA256. Actual candidate rows, before test projection, are retained per Node version. Test-only projection normalizes random UUIDs and removes only the known additional Symbol(impl) key from the request/event own-key lists. No production reflection is filtered. The initial candidate failures and subsequent successful runs are retained.
+
+Known inherited backend gap: pinned Window EventTarget/Event wrappers expose an own Symbol(impl), unlike Native requests' empty own-key list and Native events' sole isTrusted property. Their inherited generated event methods/getters also retain the existing dependency's symbol-based conversion behavior; copying that symbol can affect those inherited interfaces. This patch gives Payment-specific methods/getters strong private brands and does not claim to fix the global Window event platform. There are no proxies, hidden-ownKeys shims, prototype-grafted Host public objects, or fake instanceof hooks. The private EventTarget implementation receives a private extension for its actual handler algorithms. A separately reviewable private Window event adapter is deferred.
+
+This is a bounded no-service implementation. Interactive checkout, merchant validation, payment apps, payment responses and successful updateWith transitions are not implemented or claimed. Native's PaymentResponse prototype itself has only its constructor/tag, and its constructor throws. PaymentAddress remains absent. Arbitrary unmeasured iterator/parser edge cases and broader event-platform conformance remain outside this checkpoint. No claim of full Lightpanda replication follows from this fixture passing.
+
+Validation: test/payment-request.test.js passes 10/10 serially on Node 24.19.0, 24.22.1, and 26.13.0. It includes unchanged source assertions/nonzero harness observations, private-brand/clone failures, real creation-context checks before and after removing prototypes, cross-frame method realms and removed-frame lifetime, secure opaque-frame exclusion, and real utility/worker contexts. No heap traversal, broad suites, PureScript suite, or native rebuild was needed. Creation-context checks call the prepared real V8 sameRealm API and do not infer realm from prototypes. Existing MaxListenersExceededWarning and VM Modules warnings remain visible in the logs.
+
+Run with each prepared exact Node executable:
+
+    RED_PANDA_REFERENCE_TESTS_ROOT=/path/to/pinned/src/browser/tests node --experimental-vm-modules --test --test-concurrency=1 test/payment-request.test.js
+
+Set RED_PANDA_PAYMENT_EVIDENCE_DIR to an existing directory to retain actual candidate raw rows. Browser/world hooks are small additions; codec changes add only the four strongly registered Payment kinds to existing clone rejection. The existing DOMException helper and prepared runtime/heap artifacts are dependencies. No native source changes, new dependencies, runtime default changes, network services, or Root production edits were made by this isolated work.
+
+Integration provenance: the first isolated baseline preceded Root Crypto/Range integration. The rebased-* logs validate the final isolated currentRoot graph, preserving both integrations, on all three runtimes. final-source-sha256.json binds that tested graph, base-sha256.json binds its baseline, and initial-base-sha256.json retains the earlier baseline. Browser/world patches are rebased around the later imports and installs. The production Payment module is unchanged between these two graph checks. Retained Native probe drivers use original ../scripts and ../test relative imports; copy them and expressions to a direct repository child directory such as evidence/ when reproducing those raw reports.
